<title>USA: Global Spill to buy N.Y. recycling plant.</title>
<headline>Global Spill to buy N.Y. recycling plant.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Global Spill Management Inc said on Friday it entered into an agreement to buy Recycling Unlimited Inc, a transfer and crushing plant in Brooklyn, New York, for $3.2 million.</p>
<p>The company also said its Indigo Industries of New York Inc unit won a bid for a $1.76 million project to demolish an old department store in Hempstead, N.Y.</p>
<p>Recycling Unlimited was expected to have sales of $6 million to $8 million, with a projected pre-tax profit of about $1.5 million a year.</p>
